    {
      "id": "c0e2d0de-3e8c-49da-bdd8-529d530a1cf2",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 10,
      "shortName": "scrollregion-two-axis-scrollab",
      "title": "ScrollRegion two-axis + scrollable surface (overlay/scroll rework Part 1)",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Part 1 of the overlay/scroll rework (design: docs/overlay-design.md §\"T009 rework\"; sibling: plugin-task-ui-7/T009 owns Part 2 = overlays above the scroll + base Overlay widget). Fixes BUG C (showcase content wider than the viewport runs off-screen with no scrollbar).\n\nCURRENT STATE:\n- `ScrollRegion` (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/scroll_region.rs) is an embeddable VERTICAL-ONLY scroll viewport. It bakes `-scroll_offset` into child bounds (bounds === drawn === clickable), clips via renderer PushClip/PopClip, resets `applied_offset` in `Component::on_layout` (post-order, so the shift never compounds). Public API: `new()`, `scroll_offset() -> Signal<f32>`, `scroll_to(f32)`, `ensure_visible(Rectangle)`, `scroll_to_child(usize)`. Wheel via `Event::Scroll`; auto vertical scrollbar (theme-accent thumb, wide grab lane, control_radius). Module doc explicitly says \"v1 is vertical-only; horizontal scrolling is future work.\"\n- The SHOWCASE scrolls its whole page with a MANUAL `offset_tree(dy)` (heca-renderer/examples/showcase.rs ~L1740) — vertical only — NOT a ScrollRegion. That is why wide content has no horizontal scrollbar.\n- `Surface`/`StyleExt` (background/border/radius/glow) exist as theme-driven builders on surfaces.\n\nDESIRED STATE (extend ScrollRegion; DO NOT add a parallel widget):\n1. Two-axis scrolling. Add `ScrollAxes { Vertical (default), Horizontal, Both }` via builders `.horizontal()`/`.both()` (default Vertical = back-compat; existing callers unchanged). Per-axis offset — decision Q2 lean: keep the existing `scroll_offset()` Signal<f32> as the vertical accessor and ADD a horizontal `scroll_offset_x()` Signal<f32> (two signals, smaller diff) rather than switching to a Point. Lay children at natural size on BOTH axes (no shrink) so content overflows horizontally; bake `-offset` on both axes in the same place the vertical shift is applied; clip to the region rect (already done).\n2. Horizontal scrollbar on the bottom edge mirroring the vertical thumb (theme-accent grip, wide invisible grab lane, control_radius); auto-shown only when the horizontal axis overflows. Q1 lean: overlay/auto-hide over content (match the vertical thumb), no reserved gutter.\n3. Wheel/trackpad: plain `Event::Scroll` delta → vertical; Shift+wheel → horizontal; a 2-D delta drives both. Clamp each axis to [0, max_offset]. Confirm what `Event::Scroll` carries (dx/dy? modifiers?) in component.rs before wiring.\n4. Optional \"scrollable surface\" styling: give ScrollRegion optional `StyleExt` (background/border/radius/glow), theme-driven — a plain `ScrollRegion::new()` stays frameless, `.background(..).border(..)` makes it a scrollable panel. No hardcoded styling.\n5. Showcase adopts it: replace the manual `offset_tree` page-scroll with a root `ScrollRegion::new().both()` wrapping the content (dogfood; fixes BUG C). NB: overlays (Dialog/Select) must be hosted ABOVE this scroll — that is Part 2 (T009); until then the in-flow Dialog stays off-screen when scrolled (BUG B) — do not attempt to fix BUG B here.\n\nEDGE CASES: content smaller than viewport on an axis → no scrollbar, offset pinned 0; on_layout must reset BOTH axes' applied offsets; `ensure_visible`/`scroll_to_child` stay vertical for now (or extend if cheap); back-compat — `scroll_offset()` semantics unchanged for vertical-only callers.\n\nVERIFY INTERACTIVELY (mandatory — see the no-unverified-rendering lesson): unit-test the pure clamp/offset math; then the USER runs `cargo run -p heca-renderer --example showcase` to confirm horizontal + vertical scroll, the bottom scrollbar, Shift+wheel, and that a styled scrollable surface renders. Do NOT mark done on green unit tests alone.\n\nDOCS (both audiences, per the rule): docs/widgets.md ScrollRegion entry (new builders + horizontal scrollbar + StyleExt, native + declarative examples) + rustdoc; showcase demo section.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nWIDGET DONE + user-verified interactively. Commit c84528a (feat) + 6162a51 (planner) on branch feat/action-task-c. ScrollRegion extended to two-axis + scrollable surface (heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/scroll_region.rs): ScrollAxes/.horizontal()/.both(); scroll_offset_x/scroll_to_x; two-axis sync_shift/on_layout; horizontal scrollbar; gutter + clean corner (v_overflow/h_overflow); max_offset reserves the perpendicular gutter; click-in-track paging (both axes); StyleExt scrollable-surface; Event::Scroll two-axis (delta_x/delta_y) with host modifier→axis mapping (component.rs + select.rs + showcase). REMOVED hardcoded keys + tab-stop focusability (tmux model → keyboard scroll host-driven, T011). docs/widgets.md rewritten + rustdoc + showcase demo. Full workspace green, clippy clean, rust-skill clean. User verified two-axis pointer scroll, click-track, Shift+wheel, gutter/corner clean, plain keys don't scroll.\n\nCHECKLIST NOTE: items 1-5,7,9,10 DONE. Item 8 (user verify) DONE. Item 6 \"showcase whole-page uses ScrollRegion.both() (drop offset_tree)\" DEFERRED to Part 2 / T009 — it fully fixes BUG C but is COUPLED with overlays-above-scroll (else re-triggers BUG B: in-flow Dialog off-screen when scrolled). Forced-complete because the widget deliverable is done; the whole-page adoption belongs with the overlay rework.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
