    {
      "id": "1f73600c-1e9c-4c93-90dc-44291b137240",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 11,
      "shortName": "app-scroll-actions-prefix-gate",
      "title": "App scroll actions (prefix-gated, configurable, RPC) for the active ScrollRegion",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "App-integration follow-up to F003/P011/T010 (ScrollRegion widget). Decided with user 2026-07-16.\n\nDECISION (tmux model): plain keys (j/k/PageUp/PageDown/Home/End) CANNOT be default bindings — heca forwards plain keys to the underlying app (terminal/vim/lazygit), so binding them would steal them. Scroll defaults MUST be prefix-gated: `prefix+Home/End/PgUp/PgDn/arrows` (exact set TBD), and MUST be configurable so the end user can rebind to plain keys (e.g. plain Home/End) if they accept the terminal tradeoff. The ScrollRegion WIDGET therefore binds NO keys and is NOT focusable (done in T010): keyboard scrolling is a HOST concern.\n\nBUILD (follow the standard heca action pattern — see AGENTS.md \"Adding New Actions\"):\n- WmAction variants for scrolling the ACTIVE scroll region, e.g. ScrollLineUp/Down, ScrollPageUp/Down, ScrollHome/End (or one parameterized ScrollActive { axis, amount } — pick per the enum style). Parameterized/axis-aware for horizontal too.\n- action_from_name + build_action (if parameterized) + action_priority + handler in handlers.rs + build_registry + ActionRegistry::ALL descriptor + action_policy classification (interaction.rs) + RPC parser (rpc.rs).\n- keybindings.default.toml: prefix-gated defaults (prefix+PgDn/PgUp/Home/End/…). Configurable via config.\n- The handler resolves the ACTIVE ScrollRegion (app-side: whichever chrome region / mounted container is active) and calls its scroll API: `scroll_to`/`scroll_to_x`/`scroll_by`/`ensure_visible` / the `scroll_offset()`/`scroll_offset_x()` signals (all public on ScrollRegion). NB: ScrollRegion isn't mounted in the app yet — this task is gated on the sidebar/panels being wrapped in a ScrollRegion (the WorkspacesContainer/chrome migration). Until then there is no active region to scroll.\n- OPTIONAL: a semantic WidgetIntent::Scroll* delivered field-first (so a focused editable child consumes its raw keys first) if we want the widget to handle host-delivered scroll intents directly; otherwise the action handler calls the region API directly.\n\nVERIFY: prefix+scroll keys scroll the active region; reachable from keyboard + RPC; a focused terminal/editor still receives plain keys (not hijacked). Docs: README + keybindings.default.toml + AGENTS \"Adding New Actions\" example.",
      "notes": "",
