    {
      "id": "586953dc-a2af-45cc-8eff-f6d5441f6ece",
      "phaseId": "99d19246-1ba9-4720-9895-e70c66acf144",
      "number": 12,
      "shortName": "regression-widget-glow-only-on",
      "title": "REGRESSION: widget glow only on focused elements (lost rest-state glow)",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "Reported by user 2026-07-16 while working on F003/P011/T010. Suspected pre-existing regression in the plugin/composition-first widget refactor (NOT introduced by the ScrollRegion work). NEEDS INTERACTIVE (GPU) DIAGNOSIS — can't be seen headless.\n\nSYMPTOM: in the showcase, changing the glow-size Select ([appearance] glow_size / GlowLevel) no longer visibly affects the new/refactored widgets; user observes glow now appears ONLY on FOCUSED widgets/elements, not at rest. It used to glow at rest.\n\nDIAGNOSIS LEADS (verified in code):\n- Glow path is global: `PaintCx::scaled_glow` (heca-grid-ui/src/component.rs:~1093) scales any Glow by `theme.colors.glow_size` (radius_scale + strength_scale); `PaintCx::rect` runs every glow through it (component.rs:748). So glow_size DOES reach every widget that PASSES a glow to `rect` (or sets `style.glow` → drawn by `paint_base`).\n- Some widgets read glow_size DIRECTLY: context_menu, marker_group, key_hint, rail_cell, icon_button.\n- Showcase wiring is fine: `self.theme.colors.glow_size = self.ctl.glow.get_untracked()` each frame (showcase.rs:2286); the glow Select sets `ctl.glow` (showcase.rs:804-809). Old widgets respond, so the select→theme→scaled_glow chain works.\n- So the regression is likely: the refactored widgets stopped PASSING a rest-state glow to their surface/border draw (only pass a glow in the focused state), OR their rest glow base intensity became 0. Focus still glows (focus ring / focused-state glow), matching the user's observation.\n\nWHERE TO LOOK: the composition-first refactored widgets (Button, Item, Select, Tabs) + Badge/Tag/DockFrame — compare their paint() glow usage now vs before the refactor (git history). Check whether the surface/border draw passes `Some(Glow{..})` at REST or only when focused. The fix: restore the rest-state theme-driven glow (read from theme, per the no-hardcode rule), so glow_size scales it at rest.\n\nVERIFY: user changes the glow Select in the showcase and sees ALL widgets' glow scale at rest (not only focused ones).",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
